{"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CapturePipeline","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"How a capture card goes from plugged in to on screen.","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Essentials","generated":true,"anchor":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient"]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/headwirecapture\/capturepipeline"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every call into the capture session runs on one serial queue, owned by an actor whose executor is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that queue, so ","type":"text"},{"code":"startRunning","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which blocks until frames flow, never runs on the main thread. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"app drives it through ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient","type":"reference"},{"text":"; this article follows one card through that client’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"endpoints.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"text":"Finding the card","anchor":"Finding-the-card","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/devices","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" streams the connected external video devices. It observes the discovery","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"session’s device list, which the system updates on every plug and unplug, so there is no polling","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and no fixed delay; repeated lists are dropped. A card can show up before its format list is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"filled in, so ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/start","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" polls for the formats, every 250 ms for up to about two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"seconds, and goes on as soon as they appear.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Choosing-the-format","text":"Choosing the format"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/formats","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" returns the formats a device offers, in the order it lists them. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"first time the app opens a card, before it sets a format, it records the card’s own active format","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and frame duration as a ","type":"text"},{"code":"CardPreferredMode","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/start"},{"text":" then resolves the format with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"FormatSelection.resolve(_:in:cardPrefers:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": the person’s selection where the card offers it,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"else the preferred format, which tries the card’s own mode first and otherwise favours frame rate,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"at least 1080p, uncompressed over compressed, and 16:9. The same resolver tells Settings which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"format Automatic picked, so the sheet and the stream agree.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The session uses the "},{"code":".inputPriority","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" preset, so the device’s active format is the one applied."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The minimum and maximum frame durations are both pinned to the rate’s exact duration, 1001\/60000"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for 59.94 fps, rather than one computed from a rounded rate.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Reading the frames","anchor":"Reading-the-frames"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The session has one video data output, beside the preview layer rather than in front of it. It"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"hands each frame in turn to three consumers: the Metal presenter, the content sampler, and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"calibration recorder. Uncompressed formats arrive as the card sends them, with nothing converted."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"For a codec, the output asks the system to decode, preferring biplanar 4:2:0; where the output"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"offers no uncompressed format, the app decodes Motion JPEG, H.264, or HEVC itself. Late frames are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"discarded rather than queued.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The content sampler reads one frame on each format change and then one every two seconds, on a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"queue of its own. Each read finds where the Mac’s picture sits inside a padded frame"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/contentBounds","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"), whether the frames carry the range their pixel format claims","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/rangeReadings","type":"reference"},{"text":"), and what the frame looks like (","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/frameLooks"},{"type":"text","text":"),"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which the app uses to tell a live picture from a no-signal field. "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/recordCalibration","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"copies a small crop of every frame for the length of one calibration."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The output also counts the frames that arrive. "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/deliveredFrameRate","type":"reference"},{"text":" reports the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"rate over the last second. When two meter windows in a row deliver under 90% of the rate the card"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"was set to, and the format was chosen automatically, the session restarts once on another pixel"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"format at the same resolution and rate, skipping a format that differs only in colour range. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"format the person chose in Settings is kept."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Drawing-the-picture","text":"Drawing the picture"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CapturePreviewView","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" shows the stream. With upscaling off, the session’s own preview layer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"draws it and no frame passes through the app. The Metal path takes over for an upscaler (MetalFX,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or super resolution finished with MetalFX), for a colour correction the card’s profile calls for,"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"and for a codec the app decodes. It converts each frame on the GPU the moment it arrives and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"presents it straight away, with no display link. If the GPU stages cannot be built, or a frame","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"arrives in a layout the shader cannot read, the view falls back to the preview layer."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/FrameFeed","type":"reference"},{"text":" puts frames from outside a capture session, such as a decoded network stream,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"through the same Metal path, so scaling, the reported layout, and upscaling behave as they do for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a card.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"When-the-session-stops","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"When the session stops"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Session notifications are reduced to one ordered stream of events. An interruption is reported as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"CaptureSessionState.interrupted(device:reason:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and its end as running again. A runtime error","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or the card being unplugged tears the session down and reports a failure. After a media services","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reset the session restarts the last request from scratch, up to three times a minute; past that it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fails and the person is asked to replug the card.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"HeadwireCapture"}],"role":"article","title":"The capture pipeline","roleHeading":"Article"},"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture/documentation/HeadwireCapture/CaptureClient/contentBounds":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where the source’s picture sits inside the padded frame, emitted now and again on every change."}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/headwirecapture\/captureclient\/contentbounds","identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/contentBounds","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"contentBounds"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"attribute","text":"@Sendable"},{"kind":"text","text":" () -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScS","text":"AsyncStream"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:20HeadwireCaptureModel13ContentBoundsV","text":"ContentBounds"},{"kind":"text","text":"?>"}],"title":"contentBounds"},"doc://headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture/documentation/HeadwireCapture/CaptureClient/deliveredFrameRate":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The rate frames arrived at over the last second, emitted now and each second while frames flow."}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/headwirecapture\/captureclient\/deliveredframerate","identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/deliveredFrameRate","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"deliveredFrameRate"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"attribute","text":"@Sendable"},{"kind":"text","text":" () -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScS","text":"AsyncStream"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double"},{"kind":"text","text":"?>"}],"title":"deliveredFrameRate"},"doc://headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture/documentation/HeadwireCapture/CaptureClient/rangeReadings":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What the stream’s frames say about their pixel format’s range label, emitted now and on every change."}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/headwirecapture\/captureclient\/rangereadings","identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/rangeReadings","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"rangeReadings","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"@Sendable","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" () -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncStream","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScS"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"RangeReading","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:20HeadwireCaptureModel12RangeReadingO"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"title":"rangeReadings"},"doc://headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture/documentation/HeadwireCapture":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"External capture on iPadOS: finding a USB capture card, running it in a chosen format, and showing its video full screen."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/headwirecapture","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture","title":"HeadwireCapture"},"doc://headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture/documentation/HeadwireCapture/CapturePreviewView":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Shows the capture stream at a scaling and reports where the video and its content land."}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/headwirecapture\/capturepreviewview","identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CapturePreviewView","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"CapturePreviewView"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"CapturePreviewView"}],"title":"CapturePreviewView"},"doc://headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture/documentation/HeadwireCapture/CaptureClient/frameLooks":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/frameLooks","title":"frameLooks","url":"\/documentation\/headwirecapture\/captureclient\/framelooks","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The look of each frame the content sampler reads, about every two seconds while frames flow."}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"frameLooks","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"@Sendable","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" () -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncStream","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScS"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"FrameLook","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:20HeadwireCaptureModel9FrameLookV"},{"text":"?>","kind":"text"}]},"doc://headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture/documentation/HeadwireCapture/CaptureClient/formats":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The formats a connected device offers, in the order the device lists them."}],"role":"symbol","deprecated":true,"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/headwirecapture\/captureclient\/formats","identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/formats","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"formats","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"@Sendable","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" (","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"device","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"CaptureDevice","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:20HeadwireCaptureModel0B6DeviceV"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"ID","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:20HeadwireCaptureModel0B6DeviceV2IDa"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"CaptureFormat","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:20HeadwireCaptureModel0B6FormatV"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"title":"formats"},"doc://headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture/documentation/HeadwireCapture/CaptureClient/devices":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The connected external devices, emitted now and again on every plug or unplug."}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/headwirecapture\/captureclient\/devices","identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/devices","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"devices","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"@Sendable","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" () -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncStream","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScS"},{"text":"<[","kind":"text"},{"text":"CaptureDevice","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:20HeadwireCaptureModel0B6DeviceV"},{"text":"]>","kind":"text"}],"title":"devices"},"doc://headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture/documentation/HeadwireCapture/CaptureClient/recordCalibration":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/headwirecapture\/captureclient\/recordcalibration","title":"recordCalibration","identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/recordCalibration","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Copies "},{"code":"crop","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" out of every frame for "},{"code":"duration","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", for a calibration, and returns the copies."}],"kind":"symbol","deprecated":true,"fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"recordCalibration"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"attribute","text":"@Sendable"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"_"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"crop"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"text":"CalibrationGeometry","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:20HeadwireCaptureModel19CalibrationGeometryV"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Crop","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:20HeadwireCaptureModel19CalibrationGeometryV4CropV"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"duration","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Duration","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"CalibrationRecording","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:20HeadwireCaptureModel20CalibrationRecordingV"}]},"doc://headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture/documentation/HeadwireCapture/CaptureClient":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/headwirecapture\/captureclient","title":"CaptureClient","identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"CaptureClient","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Discovers external capture devices and streams one of them to a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CapturePreviewView"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"CaptureClient","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture/documentation/HeadwireCapture/CaptureClient/start":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/headwirecapture\/captureclient\/start","title":"start","identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/start","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Streams a device, using the selection when the device supports it and its preferred format otherwise.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","deprecated":true,"fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"start"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"attribute","text":"@Sendable"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"_"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"device"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:20HeadwireCaptureModel0B6DeviceV","text":"CaptureDevice"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:20HeadwireCaptureModel0B6DeviceV2IDa","text":"ID"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"_"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"selection"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:20HeadwireCaptureModel15FormatSelectionV","text":"FormatSelection"},{"kind":"text","text":"?) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s4Voida","text":"Void"}]},"doc://headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture/documentation/HeadwireCapture/FrameFeed":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Frames the app hands in from outside a capture session, such as a decoded network stream, for a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CapturePreviewView"},{"type":"text","text":" to draw as it draws a capture card."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/FrameFeed","url":"\/documentation\/headwirecapture\/framefeed","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"FrameFeed","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"FrameFeed","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","title":"FrameFeed","kind":"symbol"}}}